WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.1 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Workforce planning

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Match the people you will need to the work your strategy requires, starting with what you carry yourself.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
Workforce planning matches the people you will need to the work your strategy requires, over time: how much time each role needs, which skills, and from when. It starts with what you carry yourself.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Who will do the work

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:39.722
Employees: Steady time for core, ongoing work. They need a contract, pay and management. For example: The bakery hires its first part-time baker once weekly orders cover the wage.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:50.311
Contractors: Specialist skills for a defined task, often the first paid help. For example: A freelance designer builds the tutoring service's booking page for a fixed fee.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:01.270
Volunteers: Time, local knowledge and trust. Not free: they need training, supervision and expenses. For example: Retired electricians fix lamps at the repair café, with their expenses repaid.

8
00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:13.800
Interns: Fresh skills while they learn. They need a learning plan and supervision. For example: A design student spends ten weeks making the youth club's posters, with a mentor.

9
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:14.800
Why plan it now

10
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.474
1. You see how much you and your co-founders are really carrying.

11
00:01:20.474 --> 00:01:26.148
2. You fill the roles that matter most first, when money allows.

12
00:01:26.148 --> 00:01:33.193
3. You know who would cover if a founder suddenly could not work.

13
00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.193
What it guides

14
00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:39.126
1. Your recruitment, contracts and onboarding, next in this module.

15
00:01:39.126 --> 00:01:44.430
2. Your budget: what income or milestone pays for each role.

16
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:50.733
3. Your partners: which roles could be shared rather than hired.

17
00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:51.733
What to avoid

18
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:57.037
Treating volunteers as free, with no recruiting, training or expenses.

19
00:01:57.037 --> 00:02:02.341
Building the model on unpaid people doing core, ongoing work.

20
00:02:02.341 --> 00:02:09.385
Mixing up employees and contractors without checking the rules where you are.

21
00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:11.785
You draft a workforce plan for your first one to two years.

22
00:02:11.785 --> 00:02:15.785
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:17.285 --> 00:02:20.385
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
